Scott 1976, (4.18). If a and b are retracts, then second projection composed with the tensor of a and b is typed as an arrow from that tensor to b.

Typedness unfolds to the arrow equation, which rewrites by the arrow rule. Graph extensionality uses the retract equation of the tensor, then simplification by composition, the second-projection combinator, and the retract equation, followed by the tensor rule, the one projection, and the retract equation of b.
